Privileges of international organisations

19. To implement an agreement made by the Government of the Maldives with an international organisation, the Minister shall have the power to determine that the following privileges shall be available to that organisation to a specific extent determined by the Minister:

(a) privilege from legal proceedings brought against that organisation;

(b) privilege, on the same level as the privilege granted to the official archives of representatives of foreign countries who have presented credentials to the President and to premises established [?], for the official archives of that organisation and premises used as [?];

(c) exemption from, or refund of, payment of taxes and other charges, except import or export duty on goods or excise duty;

